			<div class="content" id="post-content-1826872">
									

<p>This is a rewrite of <a href="/scp-257-arc">SCP-257-ARC</a>, posted on 19 Aug 2008 by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drakerunner" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(186308); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=186308&amp;size=small&amp;timestamp=1375678030" alt="DrakeRunner" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=186308)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drakerunner" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(186308); return false;">DrakeRunner</a></span>.</p>
<p>This also bears some explanation:</p>
<p>The original SCP had been archived for being the first on-site reference of the challenge-phrase, &quot;Does the Black Moon howl?&quot;. A long-time in-joke amongst staff, my personal headcanon is that it's the trigger phrase for a small, benign memetic agent that's embedded in all staff assigned to work on mind-affecting SCPs, especially those with an occult bent to them.</p>
<p>When a mentally healthy researcher is given the trigger phrase, they will reflexively answer with the response, &quot;Only when waning.&quot; If a compromised researcher is given the trigger phrase, the embedded agent will trigger a momentary breakdown that results in all sorts of absurd responses.</p>
<hr />
<p>Edit: Other things I need to point out &#8212;</p>
<ul>
<li>If it's not clear enough, this is meant to be a parody of <a href="http://www.rpgmakerweb.com/">RPG Maker</a>. All credit where it's due.</li>
<li>It may be overly subtle, but &quot;Limited Founder's Edition&quot; is supposed to imply that this was, well, Kickstarted. As in, &quot;Pledge $1000 today and you will get a Limited Founder's Edition with steel case, art book, and a letter of thanks signed by all of the development team! (25 available)&quot;</li>
</ul>

